1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,292
Content ops means batch recording once, then many cuts.

2
00:00:03,292 --> 00:00:05,487
Do not live in endless one-offs.

3
00:00:05,487 --> 00:00:08,413
This lesson is about content that sells (ops).

4
00:00:08,413 --> 00:00:10,242
Batch recording → many cuts.

5
00:00:10,242 --> 00:00:12,802
Do not treat this as theory only.

6
00:00:12,802 --> 00:00:16,460
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

7
00:00:16,460 --> 00:00:21,947
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

8
00:00:21,947 --> 00:00:25,971
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

9
00:00:25,971 --> 00:00:30,360
Stay practical: plan one batch session before you optimize branding or tools.

10
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:34,406
Plan one batch session: topics, hooks, and a finish time.

11
00:00:34,406 --> 00:00:37,015
Remember the objective: plan one batch session.

12
00:00:37,015 --> 00:00:41,114
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

13
00:00:41,114 --> 00:00:45,586
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

14
00:00:45,586 --> 00:00:49,685
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

15
00:00:49,685 --> 00:00:54,157
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

16
00:00:54,157 --> 00:00:56,765
Talk to a real person when possible.

17
00:00:56,765 --> 00:00:58,256
Feedback beats guessing alone.

18
